WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:03.703
-The midterm elections
are coming up,

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.205
and with many citizens
still scarred

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:06.840
and needing emotional support
after 2020,

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:10.510
we turn to one of our writers,
Jeff Wright, to help voters out.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.912
Let's take a look.

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:15.147
-Alrighty, welcome
to the voter support group.

00:00:15.147 --> 00:00:16.749
As we all know,
midterms are here,

00:00:16.749 --> 00:00:18.985
and this can be a really
stressful time for voters.

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:20.286
So today we'll open up the floor

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:22.354
for you to express
your frustrations with voting.

00:00:22.354 --> 00:00:23.555
Who wants to go first?

00:00:23.555 --> 00:00:25.491
-I'll go first.
[ Clears throat ]

00:00:25.491 --> 00:00:27.527
If you couldn't tell
by my jeans and plaid shirt,

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:29.061
I'm a Republican.
-[ Booing ]

00:00:29.061 --> 00:00:31.063
-Come on, now.
-Like I was saying,

00:00:31.063 --> 00:00:33.766
I'm a Republican,
and being a Republican is hard.

00:00:33.766 --> 00:00:36.302
Everyone automatically assumes
I'm a Trump supporter.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:37.637
-Did you vote for Trump?
-I did.

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:38.538
-Come on, man.

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:39.706
-But not because
I agree with him.

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:40.940
-You don't?
-No.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:43.109
Voting is like having
a favorite football team.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:45.578
You got to stick with your team,
even if your quarterback

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:47.380
is under multiple
criminal investigations.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:48.247
-Who's your favorite
football team?

00:00:48.247 --> 00:00:49.348
-The Browns.
-[ Booing ]

00:00:49.348 --> 00:00:51.150
-Yeah, I know.
You can boo. It's fair.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:52.819
-Let's move on.
Who wants to go next?

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:55.155
-I'll go.
I'm an old voter.

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:57.056
And I don't like
that everyone can vote.

00:00:57.056 --> 00:00:58.891
It's too easy now,
and I hate it.

00:00:58.891 --> 00:01:01.294
Back in my day,
you had to work hard to vote,

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:02.795
and that vote meant something.
-Here we go again.

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:04.863
-It was a mission
to get your vote in.

00:01:04.863 --> 00:01:07.800
You had to wake up before
the sun, look for your shoes,

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.601
then realize you're
already wearing them.

00:01:09.601 --> 00:01:13.239
Oh, then I'd walk seven miles
through the snowstorm

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:15.608
with the summer sun
beaming on my back.

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:17.043
It was hot.
-Snowstorm in the summer?

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:19.512
-And don't forget the goblin
waiting in front of the booth.

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:22.415
You had to say, "Swiper,
no swiping, Swiper, no swiping."

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:23.616
And he still might not
let you in.

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:25.018
-Alright, that's all the time
you have left.

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:26.719
-Well, I vote I keep going.
-I bet you do.

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:28.287
Who wants to go next?
-I'll go.

00:01:28.287 --> 00:01:29.555
Hi, everyone.

00:01:29.555 --> 00:01:31.224
I'm a Democrat, which means
I love black people.

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:32.292
Just not in my neighborhood.

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:34.093
-Hey, I'm with you on that.

00:01:34.093 --> 00:01:36.462
-I'm tired of people thinking
just because I'm a Democrat,

00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:38.331
I would never vote
for a Republican.

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:39.965
Maybe I like what Republicans
have to offer.

00:01:39.965 --> 00:01:41.734
-Oh, what do you like
that the Republicans offer?

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:45.805
-Well, they offer
a lot of, um...

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:49.976
If you think about it,
they, uh, uh...

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:51.310
I mean, Tom Brady once said --

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:53.446
Wait, is Tom Brady a Republican
or is he just rich?

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:54.981
-And handsome.
Rich and handsome.

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:57.517
-Alright, l-let's move on.
How about you next, young voter?

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:59.152
-I'm a young voter,
which means I don't vote.

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:00.153
-[ Booing ]
-Come on, now.

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:01.354
-Hey, I thought you said
no judgment.

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:02.388
-Mnh-mnh, that deserved a boo.

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:03.822
-Alright, sorry about that.
Continue.

00:02:03.822 --> 00:02:05.491
-I just don't know
why they make it so hard.

00:02:05.491 --> 00:02:08.027
I got to stand in line
in my old high school gym

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:10.496
and use a pen like an old person
on a Tuesday.

00:02:10.496 --> 00:02:11.965
I work on Tuesdays.
-You do?

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:14.133
-I mean, I could.
I could work on Tuesdays.

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:15.201
-Come on, man.
-And besides,

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:16.469
even after an election
these days,

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:17.971
some people still
don't accept the results.

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:19.338
-Like who?
-Like him.

00:02:19.338 --> 00:02:20.740
-Hey.
-Care to chime in?

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:24.343
-Oh, no, I have plenty to say --
after the election.

00:02:24.343 --> 00:02:26.145
-[ Clears throat ]
I just want to say,

00:02:26.145 --> 00:02:27.813
when it comes to
political parties,

00:02:27.813 --> 00:02:29.481
there are bad people
on both sides.

00:02:29.481 --> 00:02:31.084
-[ Booing ]
-Shut up.

00:02:31.084 --> 00:02:32.885
-Th-There are good people
on both sides, too.

00:02:32.885 --> 00:02:34.620
-[ Booing ]
-Shut up.

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:36.255
-Okay. I guess
I'll just keep sweeping.

00:02:36.255 --> 00:02:38.390
-And I'll borrow this.

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:40.659
-Maybe as a young voter
I'd be more inclined to vote

00:02:40.659 --> 00:02:41.828
if you could do it online.

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:43.062
-See, that's y'all problem.

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:44.997
Y'all young kids
want everything online.

00:02:44.997 --> 00:02:47.300
You want to vote online.
You want your food online.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.901
You want your girlfriend online.

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:50.336
Shoot, you want Netflix online.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:51.470
-Netflix is online.

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:53.238
-Not mine.
My Netflix is on my TV.

00:02:53.238 --> 00:02:54.373
-'Cause your TV's online.

00:02:54.373 --> 00:02:55.441
-Mnh-mnh, not me.

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.443
I get my Netflix
in a little envelope.

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:58.644
Then I open it up,

00:02:58.644 --> 00:03:01.047
then I blow on it,
make sure it's still good.

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:04.050
Then I put it inside
what's called a DVD player.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.484
Y'all young kids
don't know nothing about that.

00:03:05.484 --> 00:03:06.953
-'Cause we just watch it
on our phones.

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:09.021
-Your phone?
Your phone's a DVD player?

00:03:09.021 --> 00:03:11.123
This is tricky.
Hold on. Siri!

00:03:11.123 --> 00:03:13.326
-Alright, is there anyone else
that hasn't spoken?

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:16.462
-Hi. My name is Jeff,
and I'm an alcoholic.

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:18.164
Actually, I think
I'm in the wrong room.

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:19.165
-Oh, no,
you're in the right room.

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:20.567
-Siri!

